cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite the PRML Cookbook in academic or pedagogical work, please use the form below."
title: "PRML Cookbook: Patterns and anti-patterns for using Pre-Registered ML Manifests"
abstract: >-
  A field manual for the PRML v0.1 specification. Ten patterns covering
  single-shot evals, multi-seed reporting, streaming evaluations, dataset
  pinning, CI gates, registry anchoring, revocation, infrastructure-free
  pre-registration, RLHF win-rate evaluations, and federated evaluation
  across organisations. Four anti-patterns covering common implementation
  mistakes. Four working examples (PyTorch, Stable-Baselines3, Inspect AI,
  HuggingFace lm-eval-harness).
